# FILE LAW — Website vs .oo/.oot only
File: website/audit/file-law.oot

Verdict: FAIL-CLOSED. The website repo is a JavaScript SPA.
RULES.oot §1.14 requires .oo for code and .oot for documents.
This tree does not obey that law.

## 1. Observed file types (git tree, not .git)

| Ext | Count | RULES 1.14 |
|-----|-------|------------|
| .oo | 6 | allowed (all are ANCHOR.oo) |
| .oot | 0 | none (until this audit/) |
| .js | 1 | banned outside editor extensions |
| .html | 2 | not in the allowed set |
| .css | 1 | not in the allowed set |
| .json | 8 | not in the allowed set |
| .md | 1 | only governance README.md is allowed |
| .sh | 1 | only two host scripts are allowed |
| .txt | 2 | not in the allowed set |
| .yml | 2 | GitHub Actions require YAML |
| .xml | 1 | sitemap |
| .svg / .png | 2 | binary assets |

src/main.js is the only product code. It is not .oo.
There is no .oot document that an agent can treat as the site manual.
llms.txt claims File: openOODA/LLMS.oot. That path does not exist.

## 2. Line cap (RULES 1.8, RFC-0003)

Root ANCHOR.oo states: "Every file is under 256 lines."
That sentence is false.

| File | Lines | Cap |
|------|-------|-----|
| src/main.js | 5857 | FAIL (22.8x) |
| index.html | 256 | at cap |
| styles/main.css | 218 | pass if CSS counted |
| llms.txt | 157 | pass if txt counted |
| all ANCHOR.oo | <= 46 | pass |

src/ANCHOR.oo defends the 5857-line file as "one concept".
RFC-0003 requires split along domain seams at 256.
Router, theme, markdown, and dogfight are four seams.

## 3. Academy headers (RFC-0003 §2)

Required on every product .oo: Title, Logline, Setup, Beats.
Missing Setup on: src/ANCHOR.oo, styles/ANCHOR.oo,
assets/ANCHOR.oo, .github/workflows/ANCHOR.oo.
.github/ has no ANCHOR.oo.
Root ANCHOR.oo lists a VERSION file. No VERSION file exists.
That absence matches RFC-0006. The ANCHOR text is stale.

## 4. GitHub Pages residual

GitHub Pages serves HTML. A public site needs a deploy surface
that is not .oo. Honest model:

1. Source of truth: .oot copy and .oo logic.
2. Deploy artifacts: generated HTML/CSS, marked
   `THIS FILE IS GENERATED — DO NOT EDIT` (RFC-0003 §1).
3. No hand-maintained .js.

Today the repo IS the deploy artifact. There is no generator.
oodac WASM/JS emit is out of scope this pass (gemini owns oodac).

Until a generator ships, new files in this repo must still be
.oo or .oot. Do not add more .js, .json, or .md.

## 5. install.sh

RULES.oot §1.14 allows two host scripts:
`bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` and `install.sh`.
website/install.sh is a third shell file.
It is a four-line curl-to-bash redirect to packaging/install.sh.
Keep the URL /install.sh for users. Replace the body with a
static note in .oot plus a generated redirect when a generator
exists. Do not grow this .sh.

## 6. Next repair (this repo)

1. Stop adding .js / .json / .md.
2. Split or delete src/main.js until every remaining file is
   <= 256 lines. Prefer delete of the dogfight (see spa-drag.oot).
3. Replace pulled/*.json with pulled/*.oot. Teach the loader
   later. Until then, do not add a ninth JSON file.
4. Rewrite llms.txt content as llms.oot. Keep a generated
   llms.txt at the web root only if the llmstxt.org convention
   still requires the .txt name.
